{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "bridge-api-collection",
    "name": "Postman-Xray Bridge API",
    "description": "API collection for the Postman-Xray Bridge service.\n\nThis service syncs Postman collection run results to Jira Xray for test management.\n\n## Features\n- Upload JUnit XML files and sync to Xray\n- Sync monitor runs from real Postman APIs\n- Automatic transformation to inject Xray test_key properties\n- Scheduled sync jobs to poll Postman for new runs\n- State management for incremental syncing\n\n## Setup\n1. Set the `baseUrl` variable to your bridge service URL\n2. Configure Xray credentials in the bridge service's `.env` file",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:4000",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Server Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            },
            "description": "Check if the bridge service is running and healthy."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Xray Connection",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/xray",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["health", "xray"]
            },
            "description": "Check if Xray credentials are configured and valid by attempting to authenticate."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Service health endpoints"
    },
    {
      "name": "Sync",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "JUnit XML (file upload)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": "",
                  "description": "JUnit XML file to upload"
                },
                {
                  "key": "projectKey",
                  "value": "SJP",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Jira project key"
                },
                {
                  "key": "testPlanKey",
                  "value": "SJP-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Test Plan issue key"
                },
                {
                  "key": "testExecKey",
                  "value": "",
                  "type": "text",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Optional: Existing Test Execution key to update"
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/junit",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "junit"]
            },
            "description": "Upload a JUnit XML file and sync to Xray.\n\nThe transformation extracts test keys from testsuite names (format: `SJP-X | Test Name`) and injects them as properties in each testcase."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "JUnit XML (raw body)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/xml"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<testsuites>\n  <testsuite name=\"SJP-2 | Change Order API Test\" tests=\"1\" failures=\"0\">\n    <testcase name=\"Change order submitted successfully\" time=\"0.002\"/>\n  </testsuite>\n</testsuites>"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/junit?projectKey=SJP&testPlanKey=SJP-1",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "junit"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "projectKey",
                  "value": "SJP"
                },
                {
                  "key": "testPlanKey",
                  "value": "SJP-1"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Send raw JUnit XML in the request body instead of uploading a file.\n\nOptions are passed as query parameters."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Monitor Runs",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/run",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "run"]
            },
            "description": "Sync monitor runs from real Postman Monitor APIs to Xray.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Fetch all collections from workspace (Postman API)\n2. Filter to collections with `test-plan-id` variable (Xray-linked)\n3. Get monitors for each collection (Monitor API)\n4. Fetch runs since last sync (respects SYNC_BASE_TIME)\n5. Transform and push to Xray\n\n**Body parameters:**\n- `workspaceId` (optional): Workspace ID. Uses `POSTMAN_WORKSPACE_IDS` from env if not provided.\n- `monitorId` (optional): Specific monitor/jobtemplate ID to sync. Skips collection lookup if provided.\n\n**Environment variables:**\n- `POSTMAN_WORKSPACE_IDS`: Default workspace(s) to sync\n- `SYNC_BASE_TIME`: Only sync runs after this timestamp\n- `MONITOR_API_URL`: Internal monitor API base URL\n- `DRY_RUN`: If true, pushes to Xray but skips DB updates"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Monitor Runs (specific workspace)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"workspaceId\": \"your-workspace-id\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/run",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "run"]
            },
            "description": "Sync all Xray-linked collections in a specific workspace."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Monitor Runs (specific monitor)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"monitorId\": \"your-monitor-jobtemplate-id\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/run",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "run"]
            },
            "description": "Sync a specific monitor by its jobtemplate ID. Skips the workspace/collection lookup."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Mock Sync (legacy)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/sync/run/mock",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["sync", "run", "mock"]
            },
            "description": "⚠️ Legacy endpoint using mock APIs.\n\nTrigger sync job using mock collection run API. Use `/sync/run` for real monitor sync."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Endpoints for syncing test results to Xray.\n\n- `/sync/junit` - Upload JUnit XML from Newman/CLI\n- `/sync/run` - Sync from real Postman Monitor APIs\n- `/sync/run/mock` - Legacy mock-based sync"
    },
    {
      "name": "Scheduler",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scheduler/status",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["scheduler", "status"]
            },
            "description": "Get the current status of the sync scheduler and state.\n\nReturns:\n- Whether the scheduler is running\n- Cron expression\n- Configured workspace IDs\n- Last sync timestamp\n- Recent sync jobs"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Start",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"workspaceIds\": [],\n  \"cronExpression\": \"0 * * * *\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scheduler/start",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["scheduler", "start"]
            },
            "description": "Start the automatic sync scheduler.\n\n**Body options:**\n- `workspaceIds`: Array of workspace IDs to sync (uses env config if not provided)\n- `cronExpression`: Cron schedule (default: `0 * * * *` = every hour)\n\n**Cron examples:**\n- `0 * * * *` - Every hour\n- `*/15 * * * *` - Every 15 minutes\n- `0 9 * * *` - Daily at 9 AM"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Stop",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scheduler/stop",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["scheduler", "stop"]
            },
            "description": "Stop the automatic sync scheduler."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset State",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/scheduler/reset",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["scheduler", "reset"]
            },
            "description": "Reset all sync state. The next sync will re-process all runs as if syncing for the first time.\n\n⚠️ Use with caution - this may cause duplicate test executions in Xray."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Endpoints for managing the automatic sync scheduler (cron-based)."
    }
  ]
}
